\title{gtheorytools: Tools for Generalizability Theory}
\description{
Estimates variance components for one- and two-facet G studies with crossed
or nested designs, and computes D studies with random, finite, or fixed
facets. Reports standard errors, compares D studies across sample sizes,
and selects designs that meet a target coefficient.
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=g_study]{g_study()}} fits a one- or two-facet G study.
\item \code{\link[=d_study]{d_study()}} computes a D study for one set of sample sizes.
\item \code{\link[=compare_d_studies]{compare_d_studies()}} compares D studies across combinations of facet sample sizes.
\item \code{\link[=find_d_designs]{find_d_designs()}} selects D studies that meet a G or Phi target.
}
}
